instuection set for cpu11

(0000) SCA - Prompts the user to enter an 8 bit number, sets it to the accumilator
(0001) HAL - Halts the program
(0010) LOD {d1} - Sets the accumilator to whatever $d1 is
(0011) CLR - clears and dumps the memory
(0100) TAC - sets memory address mem[1] and mem[0] (see JMP && JZE for usage) to the current counter
(0101) LDA {d1} - Copy data from memory address $d1 into Accumulator
(0110) STA {d1} - Load Accumilator into memory address $d1
(0111) ADD {d1} - adds memory contents $d1 and accum together, for example d1= 00001001 accum= 10001010, answer= 10010011
(1000) SUB {d1} - like add, but subtracts instead.
(1001) AND {d1} - Bitwise AND memory contents with Accumulator; then stores to accumilator.
(1010) ORR {d1} - Bitwise OR memory contents with Accumulator; then stores to accumilator.
(1011) JMP - Unconditionally sets the counter to mem[0] and mem[1] 
- where mem[0] is the first 8 bits of a 16 bit number and mem[1] are the latter 8.
(1100) JZE - Conditionally sets the counter to mem[0] and mem[1] 
- where mem[0] is the first 8 bits of a 16 bit number and mem[1] are the latter 8; if the Zero Flag is set.
(1110) DIF - Like DIS, but clears the screen first (and is 16x16).
(1111) DIS - takes the first 8 memory addresses (00000000-00000111) and outputs then as a display-like image,
 data inside the address is the x value, and the actual address is the y value
